WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.612
Every tool should have a narrow contract.

00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:08.947
Start with the name. Use a verb plus an object, such as search policies or get order.

00:00:08.947 --> 00:00:14.677
Then write a description that tells the model when to use the tool and when not to use it.

00:00:14.677 --> 00:00:17.692
Keep the input schema small and typed.

00:00:17.692 --> 00:00:21.426
Return structured results with provenance whenever possible.

00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:29.435
Also classify side effects. Is this tool read-only, or can it change real-world state?

00:00:29.435 --> 00:00:37.250
Finally, define policy around the tool: timeout, retry behavior, cost limits, permissions, and approval requirements.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:42.250
For example, search policy may be read-only and low risk.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:49.108
Send payment or delete record should be treated much more carefully.

00:00:49.628 --> 00:00:54.330
By default, expose the smallest set of tools needed for the current task.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.879
A smaller menu usually improves routing and reduces risk.
